WEBVTT

00:01.400 --> 00:04.220
<i>My name is Luke Braveheart.</i>

00:04.530 --> 00:08.680
<i>I was born as the legendary hero 
and I have spent my whole life fighting.</i>

00:09.300 --> 00:13.760
<i>The Voids appeared in our world, 
so in order to protect the Soul Futures,</i>

00:13.760 --> 00:15.610
<i>my friends and I fought.</i>

00:17.160 --> 00:19.790
<i>And fought. And fought.</i>

00:20.330 --> 00:25.660
<i>Then, one after another,
we lost the Soul Futures.</i>

00:27.480 --> 00:31.380
Luke, I'm leaving the world in your hands.

00:32.250 --> 00:34.350
Chingosman!

00:34.960 --> 00:36.540
<i>And then, I lost friends.</i>

00:37.310 --> 00:38.650
<i>One after another.</i>

00:39.870 --> 00:41.050
<i>After another.</i>

00:45.340 --> 00:47.600
Don't speak. You'll lose more magma.

00:58.420 --> 01:00.780
<i>And so, the Nine Soldiers became four.</i>

01:03.120 --> 01:07.370
<i>And we only have one Soul Future
 left to defend now.</i>

01:09.400 --> 01:11.240
It's the Nine Soldiers!

01:11.630 --> 01:13.490
It's the legendary hero.

01:14.200 --> 01:16.070
Great hero, show us your sword!

01:16.070 --> 01:17.670
Whoa! It's real!

01:17.670 --> 01:19.050
So cool!

01:18.130 --> 01:20.140
Legendary hero, my ass.

01:20.140 --> 01:25.140
Yeah. When are we gonna be able to go back
 to not cowering from Voids every day.

01:22.640 --> 01:25.140
Give me head pats, too.

01:35.070 --> 01:36.110
What am I...

01:37.830 --> 01:40.090
What am I even fighting for?

01:43.790 --> 01:45.990
Looks like it is just the one.

01:45.990 --> 01:47.680
All of you stay on standby here.

01:47.680 --> 01:50.290
Don't push yourself, Luke. I'll come with you.

01:50.460 --> 01:52.510
I'll go take a look first.

01:53.950 --> 01:55.180
What's that?

01:56.400 --> 01:59.050
<i>A giant clump of hair
appeared out of nowhere.</i>

01:59.050 --> 02:00.560
Natsuko Hirose.

02:01.320 --> 02:03.170
Natsuko Hirose?

02:07.840 --> 02:09.090
Go!

02:14.420 --> 02:16.740
<i>She took out that army 
of Voids in a single blow?</i>

02:17.030 --> 02:22.220
Go!

02:24.730 --> 02:27.550
<i>What in the world is this magic?</i>

02:29.040 --> 02:32.240
<i>Just what in the world is she?</i>

04:03.260 --> 04:07.720
Episode 9: HERO

04:09.570 --> 04:11.800
I've restored her stamina.

04:11.800 --> 04:15.360
I wonder if she will sleep 
for two to three days again.

04:15.360 --> 04:18.100
She at least looks human when she's asleep.

04:18.100 --> 04:21.790
That summoning magic must wear her out.

04:21.790 --> 04:23.870
She just lacks training.

04:23.870 --> 04:26.370
Would training actually affect that?

04:26.370 --> 04:27.090
Yup.

04:35.720 --> 04:37.630
<i>If I do this...</i>

04:39.410 --> 04:42.010
Mm, so good!

04:44.730 --> 04:45.760
What?

04:45.760 --> 04:47.540
No, it's nothing.

04:47.940 --> 04:49.540
Here. Eat this, too.

04:52.170 --> 04:53.270
Yummy!

04:54.460 --> 04:55.240
Yum!

04:55.240 --> 04:56.260
So good!

04:56.260 --> 04:58.600
<i>I can see her face when she's eating.</i>

04:59.450 --> 05:04.240
This move's definitely high in 
animation calories: the Dragon Suplex!

05:05.570 --> 05:08.640
All right!

05:10.120 --> 05:12.920
<i>Wait. I'm actually laughing?</i>

05:13.570 --> 05:16.960
<i>I'm fighting a Void. Why am I laughing?</i>

05:18.490 --> 05:20.410
<i>It makes no sense.</i>

05:23.530 --> 05:26.210
<i>It's still hard to see her face from the side.</i>

05:26.210 --> 05:30.640
<i>So maybe if I do this and make it like a 
Soul Future that can be seen from all angles...</i>

05:33.480 --> 05:35.480
I can't draw.

05:37.190 --> 05:40.150
<i>Maybe she has her own troubles.</i>

05:41.450 --> 05:43.350
So yummy!

05:43.800 --> 05:44.730
<i>Or not.</i>

05:49.110 --> 05:51.390
What <i>is</i> this? It's so frickin' good!

05:56.120 --> 05:58.870
The most important thing is 
to take care of your hair daily.

05:58.870 --> 06:01.660
You're as beautiful as ever.

05:58.870 --> 06:02.280
Memmeln, how does that hairstyle work?

06:01.660 --> 06:03.370
Do you have a routine?

06:02.280 --> 06:03.370
Excuse me?

06:07.850 --> 06:09.640
What are you doing?

06:09.640 --> 06:13.530
Natsuko will be up soon, so I'm making soba.

06:13.530 --> 06:14.760
"Soba"?

06:14.760 --> 06:19.430
It's a food from the Kingdom of Reality. 
Natsuko mentioned wanting to eat some.

06:19.430 --> 06:20.760
I see.

06:23.020 --> 06:24.810
So good!

06:24.810 --> 06:29.170
I never thought I'd get
to eat soba in the Last Town.

06:29.170 --> 06:30.540
It's super good.

06:32.900 --> 06:35.160
Luke, you must be in love...

06:35.160 --> 06:35.740
Huh?

06:35.740 --> 06:38.340
...with watching people 
eat things they find delicious.

06:38.190 --> 06:42.640
It's <i>so</i> good. Oh, wait, wasabi. 
I wish I had some wasabi.

06:38.990 --> 06:44.140
<i>Oh, I see. So I love watching people
 eat things they find delicious?</i>

06:45.240 --> 06:46.770
Yummy!

06:46.770 --> 06:49.380
What <i>is</i> this? 
I've never had anything like it!

06:49.750 --> 06:52.530
<i>No, it's not just that.</i>

06:53.600 --> 06:56.800
<i>What is this feeling?</i>

06:57.060 --> 06:58.350
<i>More importantly...</i>

06:59.820 --> 07:01.310
<i>When it comes to Natsuko...</i>

07:04.830 --> 07:06.810
<i>I could just watch her all the time.</i>

07:07.440 --> 07:09.280
<i>I find my eyes following her.</i>

07:11.060 --> 07:13.710
<i>I get anxious when she's not around.</i>

07:14.240 --> 07:16.370
<i>Whenever she seems close to someone...</i>

07:17.170 --> 07:18.750
<i>I end up shocked.</i>

07:18.750 --> 07:22.830
<i>Damn. What's with you, Natsuko Hirose?</i>

07:22.830 --> 07:24.960
<i>Natsuko Hirose!</i>

07:26.500 --> 07:29.890
<i>Natsuko Hirose!</i>

07:33.040 --> 07:36.480
Tomorrow, I'll make a pie with 
some basil. Natsuko likes that.

07:38.600 --> 07:41.290
What am I even doing?

07:45.310 --> 07:49.490
<i>No matter what I'm doing, 
I can't stop thinking about her.</i>

08:00.030 --> 08:01.080
<i>Ugh!</i>

08:01.330 --> 08:02.580
<i>What's with you...</i>

08:03.140 --> 08:08.600
<i>Natsuko Hirose?!</i>

08:08.790 --> 08:10.500
I love you.

08:11.340 --> 08:12.180
Huh?

08:13.240 --> 08:16.890
A spring of hot water? 
So they're called hot springs, huh?

08:17.150 --> 08:18.950
How am I going to take her there?

08:18.950 --> 08:21.410
I can't exactly ask Unio.

08:21.410 --> 08:23.200
Hm...

08:23.200 --> 08:26.140
I think I've been through 
what you're experiencing before.

08:26.140 --> 08:27.590
First love.

08:28.900 --> 08:30.400
First love?

08:30.400 --> 08:33.040
Hm? Is it not?

08:33.650 --> 08:36.220
Um, I don't really know.

08:36.710 --> 08:40.170
I've never felt this way 
towards anyone before.

08:41.170 --> 08:43.140
First love?

08:44.620 --> 08:46.130
<i>You appeared...</i>

08:47.130 --> 08:48.820
<i>and the whole world changed.</i>

08:49.870 --> 08:52.130
<i>Why am I fighting?</i>

08:53.630 --> 08:54.710
<i>It's for you.</i>

08:57.180 --> 08:58.740
<i>It's for you...</i>

09:00.670 --> 09:02.330
<i>that I'm defeating these Voids.</i>

09:05.310 --> 09:06.560
Squee!

09:06.560 --> 09:08.010
Natsuko Hirose!

09:11.230 --> 09:15.360
I love you!

09:26.590 --> 09:29.840
<i>This is my first love.</i>

09:36.130 --> 09:38.310
<i>Luke loves me?</i>

09:38.790 --> 09:40.080
<i>I...</i>

09:49.250 --> 09:50.250
Good morning.

09:50.560 --> 09:52.820
M-M-M-M-Morning.

09:53.490 --> 09:54.540
So hey...

09:54.540 --> 09:55.200
Huh?

09:55.200 --> 09:58.230
Let's go someplace together again.

09:58.230 --> 09:59.190
Just the two of us.

10:03.200 --> 10:04.540
How wonderful...

10:05.070 --> 10:06.960
it must be to be young.

10:06.960 --> 10:08.680
U-Um, I, uh...

10:08.680 --> 10:12.510
Luke! You promised you'd go to 
a party with me today, remember?

10:12.510 --> 10:14.600
Huh? I never promised that.

10:14.600 --> 10:18.080
Yuh-huh! We're going to a party! 
There'll be lots of cute girls there!

10:18.080 --> 10:20.100
No, really. You never mentioned it.

10:22.600 --> 10:24.590
Nope, you already promised!

10:24.590 --> 10:26.240
But you always go by yourself.

10:26.240 --> 10:27.640
I do <i>not</i> go alone.

10:27.640 --> 10:28.440
Oh, come on.

10:28.440 --> 10:30.070
I only go with you, Luke!

10:30.070 --> 10:30.810
Really?

10:30.810 --> 10:33.840
Yeah, really! I only go with you, Luke.
 So you're going, right?

10:31.380 --> 10:33.840
Natsuko, aren't you going to eat?

10:33.840 --> 10:35.100
I need a bit more sleep.

10:33.840 --> 10:36.280
I can't. I decided I'd make nikujaga today.

10:36.280 --> 10:37.610
The heck is "nikujaga"?

10:44.480 --> 10:45.870
I'm coming in.

10:46.200 --> 10:48.360
You should eat something.

10:48.360 --> 10:50.870
I have brought you 
some freshly picked fruit.

10:50.870 --> 10:52.760
<b>To\h\h
Natsuko
Hirose</b>

10:50.870 --> 10:52.760
<b>Kametaro
Tsuruyama</b>

10:51.740 --> 10:52.960
Thanks.

10:52.760 --> 10:52.960
<b>To\h\h
Natsuko
Hirose</b>

10:52.760 --> 10:52.960
<b>Kametaro
Tsuruyama</b>

10:52.960 --> 10:53.220
<b>To\h\h
Natsuko
Hirose</b>

10:52.960 --> 10:53.220
<b>Kametaro
Tsuruyama</b>

10:53.220 --> 10:53.550
<b>To\h\h
Natsuko
Hirose</b>

10:53.220 --> 10:53.550
<b>Kametaro
Tsuruyama</b>

10:53.550 --> 10:53.800
<b>To\h\h
Natsuko
Hirose</b>

10:53.550 --> 10:53.800
<b>Kametaro
Tsuruyama</b>

10:53.800 --> 10:53.920
<b>To\h\h
Natsuko
Hirose</b>

10:53.800 --> 10:53.920
<b>Kametaro
Tsuruyama</b>

10:53.920 --> 10:54.090
<b>To\h\h
Natsuko
Hirose</b>

10:53.920 --> 10:54.090
<b>Kametaro
Tsuruyama</b>

10:54.090 --> 10:55.250
<b>To\h\h
Natsuko
Hirose</b>

10:54.090 --> 10:55.250
<b>Kametaro
Tsuruyama</b>

10:56.250 --> 10:59.140
What did she mean by "Luke's demise"?

11:02.750 --> 11:07.640
That bird said, "This film's ending
 is already set in stone."

11:07.970 --> 11:09.940
What did she mean by that?

11:16.410 --> 11:17.940
Today's weather is sunny.

11:18.280 --> 11:20.700
There is 0% chance of precipitation.

11:21.940 --> 11:24.950
I'm really good at forecasting the weather.

11:24.950 --> 11:30.340
If something about the future is 
worrying you, I might be of some help.

11:30.550 --> 11:34.940
If something is troubling you, 
please don't try to bear the burden alone.

11:37.700 --> 11:39.190
This world...

11:40.170 --> 11:42.310
is the movie, <i>A Tale of Perishing</i>.

11:43.020 --> 11:44.850
And in that story...

11:44.850 --> 11:46.700
Unio dies.

11:46.700 --> 11:47.430
Huh?

11:48.230 --> 11:50.510
When that Void army
surrounded the Last Town...

11:50.940 --> 11:53.940
In the movie, Unio casts a self-destruct
 spell, sacrificing himself.

11:55.270 --> 11:57.650
Luke gets depressed, but meets Destiny,

11:57.650 --> 12:00.530
and the wound in his heart 
starts to heal, little by little.

12:00.530 --> 12:04.150
But Destiny gets engaged to the chairman
 for the sake of the children.

12:04.150 --> 12:09.250
And during a battle, Luke kills Memmeln after
 she disguises herself as the Ultimate Void.

12:13.140 --> 12:14.070
Pardon?

12:14.410 --> 12:16.550
What? Unio dies?

12:16.550 --> 12:17.790
And then, Destiny...

12:18.190 --> 12:19.850
Hm? "Kills"?

12:20.210 --> 12:20.920
Huh?

12:21.210 --> 12:23.070
Luke kills Memmeln?

12:25.190 --> 12:30.070
Memmeln gets tired of living 
and tries to end the world.

12:30.070 --> 12:32.070
But that's... Huh? But...

12:32.340 --> 12:34.680
Luke, who killed one of the Nine Soldiers.

12:34.680 --> 12:37.310
Destiny, who seduced the legendary hero.

12:37.690 --> 12:40.380
The pair become hated by everyone in town.

12:41.420 --> 12:42.550
They're cornered.

12:47.860 --> 12:49.460
S-Save me!

12:51.170 --> 12:53.190
Destiny, go on ahead.

12:55.050 --> 12:56.160
Luke!

13:02.340 --> 13:04.000
Mommy!

13:11.750 --> 13:12.720
Destiny!

13:22.410 --> 13:23.670
Destiny?

13:29.780 --> 13:34.540
Please protect... the Soul Future...

13:38.700 --> 13:40.830
Destiny is killed by a Void.

13:50.050 --> 13:52.420
All to protect this stupid thing?

13:53.070 --> 13:55.800
Why did everyone have to die for that?

13:58.860 --> 14:01.330
It's all your fault.

14:02.450 --> 14:07.420
It's all your fault!

14:27.590 --> 14:30.170
Luke is actually the Ultimate Void.

14:31.060 --> 14:34.430
And then, the world is destroyed.

14:36.730 --> 14:38.130
No...

14:39.030 --> 14:41.740
That's how the version of 
<i>A Tale of Perishing</i> I saw goes.

14:42.860 --> 14:44.230
Just like the director said...

14:44.240 --> 14:47.700
<b>To\h\h
Natsuko
Hirose</b>

14:44.240 --> 14:47.700
<b>Kametaro
Tsuruyama</b>

14:44.890 --> 14:47.400
If the ending is already set in stone...

14:47.700 --> 14:48.990
<b>To\h\h
Natsuko
Hirose</b>

14:47.700 --> 14:48.990
<b>Kametaro
Tsuruyama</b>

14:54.000 --> 14:58.840
But that is a future in a world 
where you don't exist, right, Natsuko?

14:59.250 --> 15:03.100
Luke has changed so much 
ever since you arrived, Natsuko.

15:03.100 --> 15:05.260
I have never seen him like that.

15:05.260 --> 15:09.510
Knowing you, Natsuko, you might 
even be able to change the future.

15:10.170 --> 15:11.500
You think so?

15:11.500 --> 15:12.770
I do.

15:12.770 --> 15:15.390
The possibility of a happy future...

15:15.390 --> 15:18.640
Beepity beep! It's 100%!

15:19.500 --> 15:21.560
Yay!

15:21.560 --> 15:23.010
Talk about lighthearted.

15:23.010 --> 15:25.600
It will be all right, Natsuko.

15:25.600 --> 15:28.060
Yeah. Thanks, QJ.

15:28.060 --> 15:30.860
Oh, please keep this a secret
 from everyone else.

15:30.860 --> 15:34.500
Of course. This is our little secret, Natsuko.

15:34.500 --> 15:38.330
Oh, by the way, 
what happens to me in that future?

15:38.330 --> 15:42.080
You're the only one of the 
Nine Soldiers who survives to the end.

15:42.080 --> 15:44.420
Huh? Only I survive to the end?

15:44.420 --> 15:47.180
But I mean, the world ends, so...

15:47.180 --> 15:50.960
Hey! Come on! 
That future is <i>never</i> happening!

15:52.350 --> 15:53.670
I guess you're right.

15:55.710 --> 15:58.470
Void response! Void response!

16:01.220 --> 16:02.220
Hey, that thing...

16:03.250 --> 16:04.630
It showed up before.

16:10.730 --> 16:11.650
Huh?

16:16.660 --> 16:18.500
What? The town!

16:18.500 --> 16:20.920
Damn it. Another new type?

16:20.920 --> 16:22.140
Luke!

16:26.670 --> 16:28.090
Luke!

16:29.080 --> 16:30.580
What the heck are they?

16:30.910 --> 16:34.090
They look like those things Natsuko drew.

16:36.320 --> 16:37.280
<i>No way.</i>

16:37.680 --> 16:40.240
I'll take care of the two on land first.

16:40.240 --> 16:43.930
Natsuko, Unio, Memmeln. 
Protect the city from the air raid.

16:43.930 --> 16:44.960
Roger!

16:44.960 --> 16:47.950
QJ, back them up until Natsuko's
 able to use her summoning spell.

16:47.950 --> 16:49.190
Understood.

16:49.190 --> 16:50.030
Natsuko!

16:50.030 --> 16:50.770
Huh?

16:50.770 --> 16:51.730
Are you all right?

16:52.040 --> 16:52.820
Uh, yeah.

16:52.820 --> 16:53.740
Let's go.

16:54.570 --> 16:56.020
<i>What's going on?</i>

16:56.650 --> 16:59.900
<i>The Voids are copying the things I drew?</i>

17:37.780 --> 17:40.650
Draw. You need to draw, Natsuko.

17:40.650 --> 17:41.950
I know, okay?

17:42.540 --> 17:44.100
What do I do? What do I do?

17:44.100 --> 17:46.160
Aerial battle. Aerial battle.

17:46.160 --> 17:49.170
Oh, I know. A fighter jet.

17:49.170 --> 17:50.490
I'll draw a fighter jet.

18:19.110 --> 18:20.610
<i>Something no one else can copy.</i>

18:24.410 --> 18:26.830
<i>Something no one can imitate.</i>

18:28.730 --> 18:32.780
Natsuko! Are you almost done? 
I'm reaching my limit!

18:52.580 --> 18:54.010
Unio!

18:57.520 --> 19:01.790
Shigidoro Notimagiya Kaphyu...

19:01.790 --> 19:03.210
The self-destruct spell?

19:03.210 --> 19:04.190
But that's—

19:04.830 --> 19:06.950
<i>What do I do? What do I do?</i>

19:08.950 --> 19:10.700
<i>They're all going to die!</i>

19:10.700 --> 19:12.170
It's no use.

19:12.170 --> 19:14.160
<i>Ugh, damn it!</i>

19:19.930 --> 19:20.920
Huh?

19:31.210 --> 19:32.240
Unio!

19:32.550 --> 19:34.650
<i>I have to draw something new.</i>

19:35.070 --> 19:37.580
<i>Something no one else can copy.</i>

19:38.200 --> 19:42.320
Even if you try to fix all 
of my movie, it's no use.

20:03.860 --> 20:04.920
What?

20:28.690 --> 20:29.690
Natsuko!

20:29.690 --> 20:30.910
Ow.

20:32.130 --> 20:33.580
My desk.

20:38.340 --> 20:39.660
Natsuko.

20:40.780 --> 20:43.660
Make sure we get a happy ending.

20:43.660 --> 20:46.920
I know you'll be able to change the future.

20:48.250 --> 20:49.430
QJ?

20:58.950 --> 21:00.540
QJ?

21:36.620 --> 21:40.930
QJ!

21:56.040 --> 21:57.200
Natsuko!

21:59.020 --> 22:00.950
It's my fault.

22:05.610 --> 22:06.910
It's all...

22:09.610 --> 22:11.350
my fault.

23:50.030 --> 23:54.940
<b>Episode 10: CHAOS</b>
